  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 240 AM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nThursday and Friday...Several of the latest models try to propagate \nthe upstream upper trof seen currently on water vapor imagery acrs \neastern ID, toward the upper MS RVR Valley by Thu evening battling \nridge complex along the way. This wave will try to sweep in a band \nof showers from the west Thu and into Thu night, but lingering ridge \neffects and dry air in place should erode most of the precip as it \ntries to enter the western CWA. We may just have debris clouds \nspilling in from the west off this process ruining a mostly sunny \nforecast for the day. If the clouds arn't too thick, Thu highs may \nbe a degree or two milder than Wednesday. Low temps Thu night \ngenerally in the 50s with a few upper 40s possible. Friday will look \nto be similar to Thursday or maybe continuing to trend a bit warmer \nif we get the cloud breaks and some insolation. But the next salvo \nof upper trof energy from the southwestern U.S. will pummel it's way \nnortheastward and take aim at the ridging in place. Moisture \nadvecting processes although not great, are there a little bit more \nfor the synoptic scale forcing to try and bring in at least a few \nlight showers from the west either late Friday night or Saturday, \nespecially along and west of the MS RVR.\n\nSaturday through Tuesday...Part of the incoming trof overhead may \ntranslate to more clouds and a few showers acrs the area Saturday \nputting a damper on high temp potential and they may be held well \ndown in the 60s. The latest medium range ensembles then suggest the \nupper system to erode/fill in enough for less impact and more \nsunshine/drier conditions to allow for a warming Sunday with more \nareas in the 70s. Lingering ridging and some LLVL return flow should \nkeep the dry and warming trends going into Monday, while an inland \nstriding longer wave trof drawing western Gulf moisture looms off to \nthe west. Thus another wet system may be eventually on tap acrs the \nmid CONUS by early to mid next week.",
